# a-sortie-played-out — plan 28 S4, and the OTHER half of the pair.
#
# `a-sortie-cut-short.keys` is the same base left at once; this one is
# the same base worked.  ⚠ **They are NOT one token apart and this file
# says so**: staying requires a tower, a wave and a drive out to the
# bodies, so the pair is *the same base played two ways* rather than
# `plans/12` § B7's single-token control.  What is held equal is the
# ground, the core, the spawn and the opening wallet.
#
# ⚠⚠ **THE READING: what a sortie was WORTH**, which no measurement in
# dryopea could take before the scramble existed.  Every other clock in
# the corpus counts down to a base FALLING; this one counts what the
# player carried out, and `DESIGN.md` § 14 makes that the whole
# difference between a good run and a bad one.
#
# ⚠ **Nothing ends the base but the player** (`@X293`) — the wave runs,
# the wallet moves, and the run continues until somebody drives onto the
# core and stays for six seconds.

echo a sortie played out: stay, collect, and leave with more

do toggle_mode
do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 12 0
marker 12 0 spawn 3
count markers 2 2
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -4 -2 14 -2
drag -4 -1 14 -1
drag -4 0 14 0
drag -4 1 14 1
drag -4 2 14 2
count painted 95 95

park 4 0
launched no
wallet 200 200

# ── The difference ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ A tower, so that something dies; a wave, so that something comes;
# and a player who drives OUT to collect what fell before going home.
do toggle_mode
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
click 6 0
marker 6 0 tower
do toggle_mode
top 6 0 on

wave 5
count alive 5 5
tick 40

# The tower has been working.  Park on the heap and clear it — salvage
# is the run's only income (`plans/13` V3).
drive 9 0
tick 30
park 9 0
tick 60

# ── And THEN leave ──────────────────────────────────────────────
drive 0 0
launch 90
launched yes

# ⚠⚠ **225.3 against the cut-short sortie's 200.0 — the player earned
# +25.3 points by staying**, and paid 133 ticks for them.  That is
# `DESIGN.md` § 2's *hold longer for more haul; launch now to keep what
# you have* as a number, and it is the first time dryopea has been able
# to take one: every other clock in the corpus measures a base FALLING.
wallet 225.0 225.7
ticks 140 148
